// combatfix_sites.h - the byte edits of combatfix (shared by combatfix.c and the Linux tests in test/)
// ModProjectileDynamics::doCollision (Mac 0x101d452b0, Windows DOW2.exe 0x99a220 + 0x9984c0 "does the step pass the
// target"): Windows (MSVC /fp:fast) adds |next - pos|^2 as (dy^2 + dz^2) + dx^2, |target - pos|^2 as (dz^2 + dy^2) + dx^2 and
// the dot product dir . (target - pos) as (nz*cz + ny*cy) + nx*cx; the port in source order (x, y, z). In place, same length.
// The hit point is then target offset * the hit entity's matrix: Windows inlines it as x' = ((z*Zx + y*Yx) + x*Xx) + Px,
// y' = ((x*Xy + z*Zy) + y*Yy) + Py, z' = ((x*Xz + z*Zz) + y*Yz) + Pz; the port calls the shared Vector3f::operator*=(Matrix43f)
// (source order) - that one call is redirected to combatfix_vecmat_docollision.
// v12, SimEngine collision (Windows SimEngine.dll vs the port, both run side by side on 1M random cases each):
//  - MathCollision::FindIntersection(OBBf, Segmentf) differs in 18% of the cases (hit point / normal / t), segment vs triangle
//    (CollisionModel::Query) in 13% (0.7% hit vs miss), the 4x3 inverse (CollisionModel::SetTransform / GetOBB2f,
//    QueryEntities) in 52% (the translation row): these three run as SimEngine.dll's own code, lifted to C (lift/lift.py).
//  - Mesh::TransformMesh (collision meshes are moved by inverse(old) then new at every SetTransform, so the error stays in
//    the mesh): Windows adds x' = (z*Zx + y*Yx) + x*Xx, y' = (x*Xy + z*Zy) + y*Yy, z' = (x*Xz + z*Zz) + y*Yz.
//  - CollisionSystem::QueryEntities(Segmentf): the segment into the entity's model space (inverse, then (z+y)+x orders),
//    the hit back to world space, |dir| = (y^2 + z^2) + x^2, |hit - start|^2 = (z^2 + y^2) + x^2.
//  - CollisionModel::Query: |hit - start|^2 = (z^2 + y^2) + x^2 and the triangle normal's length (nz^2 + ny^2) + nx^2.
